==English==
===Etymology===
{{compound|tax|payer|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who is [[subject]] to, [[liable]] for, or [[pay]]s [[tax]] as opposed to a nontaxpayer who is neither the subject nor the object of revenue laws
# All of the people, [[collectively]], in a population who pay tax (especially used in the context of the [[government]] financing something using the tax revenue)
#: ''The bank was [[bail out|bailed out]] by the '''taxpayer'''''.

